# /etc/pmount.allow
# pmount will allow users to additionally mount all devices that are
# listed here.
#
# This file contains a list of device names (basename only, e.g. sdb1)
# or device match patterns that pmount is permitted to mount for
# unprivileged users. If this file is empty or does not exist, pmount
# restricts mounting to the devices listed in the internal default
# allow list (usually removable media).
#
# Each line should contain a single device name or a wildcard pattern.
# Lines starting with # are ignored.

{#
  Schema for pmount has no configurable fields; the default behavior
  is controlled by the package defaults and udev rules. If a future
  schema adds an allowlist field, it would be used here.
#}